															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2104082); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2104082&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795190" alt="ManyMeats" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2104082)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2104082); return false;" >ManyMeats</a></span> <span class="odate time_1597503954 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Aug 2020 15:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4748186">
									

<p>Hello author,</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I'm&nbsp;going&nbsp;to&nbsp;just&nbsp;rapid-fire&nbsp;some&nbsp;thoughts&nbsp;here...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Return</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is kind of fun and there's definitely something here but the sum total of the details is just lacking a bit of cohesion for me. It doesn't quite &quot;come together&quot; if you will.</p>
<p>For starters, stuff like&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>approximately 560.5km in diameter.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You're talking about an area, and then to say approximately but go to the &quot;.5&quot; at this level seems silly.</p>
<p>There's just a general lack of precision in the language throughout this piece that, if corrected, would cement this a lot. The big table in the Description is more or less useless with all the black boxes. All you wanted to convey was which ones are neutralized, you didn't need to gum up the screen with a big patch of redacted info.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Three minutes after a boxer has entered its region of the ocean, SCP-5916 will become hostile and immediately accelerate towards the intruder at speeds in excess of Mach 20.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Three minutes? Why get specific here? The fact that it's 3 minutes doesn't seem to actually matter. You can just say &quot;shortly after&quot; and we come out the same on the other side.</p>
<p>I'd also point out that moving through the water at Mach 20 would kill every living thing in the ocean across the entirety of planet Earth. Mach 20 is so inconceivably fast that I'm not sure you understand. Traveling at Mach 20 would allow a person to circumnavigate the entire planet in less than 2 hours. I think you're going for &quot;really fast&quot; here, and in your rush to convey that you've introduced something so hyperbolic my suspension of disbelief is shattered.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Yung: You mean 5916-9?</p>
<p>5916-10: Little punk thought he could take me with a sucker punch. Showed him.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How does this -10 know who -9 is? That's our designation not theirs.</p>
<p>Too many errors here; this could do with a few more passes for critique and SP&amp;G. You're 80-90% of the way there in my estimation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

